ludes multiparticipant processes, interoperability, open technologies, open data, digital literacy, improved infrastructure, and online public services, as part Capítulo IV of internet governance guidelines that apply within BRASIL.\n\nThe country's role includes being referenced as the jurisdiction for internet governance discussions, regulation, oversight, and policy formulation; the document frames standards for internet regulation and data privacy within Brazil’s juridical space. The LGPD is the backbone of data protection in BRASIL, defining territorial scope, cross-border data transfer rules, localization obligations, and regulatory enforcement by ANPD. In sum, BRASIL provides the national legal framework for internet rights, privacy, data protection, data flows, and governance, with a robust system of agencies and processes to ensure compliance and public literacy in digital governance."}, "metrics": {"attempted_request_count": 1, "successful_response_count": 0, "failed_response_count": 0, "responses_with_tokens": 1, "prompt_tokens": 1369, "completion_tokens": 2304, "total_tokens": 3673, "compute_duration_seconds": 12.163898229598999, "streaming_responses": 0, "retries": 0, "requests_with_retries": 0}}}